  "content": "<p>Operations define how HAX talks to a provider. Each app's <code>connection.operations</code> object supports a required <code>browse</code> operation and an optional <code>add</code> operation.</p>\n<a11y-collapse heading-button=\"heading-button\">\n<h2 slot=\"heading\">Common operation fields</h2>\n<div slot=\"content\">\n<ul>\n<li><strong>method</strong> — HTTP method (<code>GET</code>, <code>POST</code>, etc).</li>\n<li><strong>endPoint</strong> — path appended to <code>connection.url</code> after a <code>/</code> (no leading slash).</li>\n<li><strong>data</strong> — request query values, merged over <code>connection.data</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>resultMap</strong> — path mappings from the provider response into HAX preview/gizmo data.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</a11y-collapse>\n<a11y-collapse heading-button=\"heading-button\">\n<h2 slot=\"heading\">Browse-only fields</h2>\n<div slot=\"content\">\n<ul>\n<li><strong>search</strong> — search inputs. Only the first key is used: Merlin's \"Search &lt;app title&gt;\" command sends the user's text as that query parameter. Further keys, and the legacy <code>format</code> / <code>items</code> / <code>slot</code> / <code>component</code> hints, are not rendered by current HAX, so put fixed filters in <code>data</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>pagination</strong> — <code>{ style: \"page\" | \"offset\" | \"link\", props: {...} }</code>. Stored but not used by any HAX UI today.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</a11y-collapse>\n<h2>Browse operation</h2>\n<p><code>browse</code> is the standard operation for searching and selecting media.</p>\n<code-sample type=\"json\" copy-clipboard-button=\"copy-clipboard-button\">\n<template>\n{\n  \"browse\": {\n    \"method\": \"GET\",\n    \"endPoint\": \"search\",\n    \"pagination\": {\n      \"style\": \"page\",\n      \"props\": {\n        \"previous\": \"prevPageToken\",\n        \"next\": \"nextPageToken\",\n        \"total_items\": \"pageInfo.totalResults\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"search\": {\n      \"q\": {\n        \"title\": \"Search\",\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"data\": {\n      \"part\": \"snippet\",\n      \"type\": \"video\",\n      \"maxResults\": \"20\"\n    },\n    \"resultMap\": {\n      \"defaultGizmoType\": \"video\",\n      \"items\": \"items\",\n      \"preview\": {\n        \"title\": \"snippet.title\",\n        \"details\": \"snippet.description\",\n        \"image\": \"snippet.thumbnails.default.url\",\n        \"id\": \"id.videoId\"\n      },\n      \"gizmo\": {\n        \"title\": \"snippet.title\",\n        \"description\": \"snippet.description\",\n        \"id\": \"id.videoId\",\n        \"_url_source\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=&lt;%= id %&gt;\",\n        \"caption\": \"snippet.description\",\n        \"citation\": \"snippet.channelTitle\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n</template>\n</code-sample>\n<h2>Add operation</h2>\n<p><code>add</code> is used for upload/create flows, for example local file upload in HAXCMS integrations.</p>\n<code-sample type=\"json\" copy-clipboard-button=\"copy-clipboard-button\">\n<template>\n{\n  \"add\": {\n    \"method\": \"POST\",\n    \"endPoint\": \"system/saveFile\",\n    \"acceptsGizmoTypes\": [\"image\", \"video\", \"audio\", \"pdf\", \"svg\", \"document\", \"csv\"],\n    \"resultMap\": {\n      \"item\": \"data.file\",\n      \"defaultGizmoType\": \"image\",\n      \"gizmo\": {\n        \"source\": \"url\",\n        \"id\": \"uuid\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n</template>\n</code-sample>\n<p>An <code>add</code> operation needs <code>acceptsGizmoTypes</code>, or the app is never offered as an upload target. <code>*</code> means \"files HAX can't classify,\" not \"everything.\"</p>"
}